IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-claims`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-claims (regs 77 and 77.1). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1397-1430), beside each assertion, before the run. Every date that the text does not state (the periods of s 22(2) and 23(2), the waiting period,
-- the days reg 77.1 comes into force and ceases to have effect) is invented for the test.

§ `Reg 77(1) and 77.1(1) - the purposes`

#ASSERT `reg 77(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 1` EQUALS "assessing the cost, the validity of payment, the operational impact and the effect on customer service to claimants of exempting them from the requirement in sections 49 and 50 of the Act to make periodic claims for benefits"
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 5` EQUALS "assessing the effect of allowing claimants who are entitled to benefits for one or more weeks for which they receive or are entitled to receive an indemnity payment described in paragraph 35(2)(f) to choose not to be paid benefits for those weeks"

§ `Reg 77(2) - condition of entitlement and period of eligibility (src:1399-1404)`

#ASSERT `reg 77(2) condition of entitlement to benefits` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(2) condition of entitlement to benefits` FALSE)

-- The argument order is: the waiting period; claims benefits for pregnancy; the period of s 22(2) with any extension; claims benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child; the period of s 23(2).
-- Pregnancy only: the waiting period (March 2 to 15, 1997) lies inside the period of s 22(2) (February 2 to August 2, 1997): the aggregate runs February 2 to August 2, 1997.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 3 15)) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)) FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 8 3), (YMD 1998 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1997 8 2))
-- A waiting period that begins before the period of s 22(2) pulls the start back to December 1, 1996.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 12 1), (YMD 1996 12 14)) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)) FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 8 3), (YMD 1998 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 12 1), (YMD 1997 8 2))
-- A new-born or adopted child only: the waiting period (September 7 to 20, 1997) and the period of s 23(2) (August 3, 1997 to August 1, 1998).
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 9 7), (YMD 1997 9 20)) FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 8 3), (YMD 1998 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 8 3), (YMD 1998 8 1))
-- Both kinds: from the earlier start to the later end, the waiting period counted once.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 3 15)) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 8 3), (YMD 1998 8 1)) EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1998 8 1))
-- Neither kind of benefit is claimed: no aggregate.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(i)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 3 15)) FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 2 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)) FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 8 3), (YMD 1998 8 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) apprenticeship: the period of attendance is the period of eligibility, when the course is an apprenticeship course or program.
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(ii)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 9 1), (YMD 1997 10 24)) TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 9 1), (YMD 1997 10 24))
#ASSERT `reg 77(2) the period of eligibility for the benefits referred to in subparagraph 77(3)(d)(ii)` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 9 1), (YMD 1997 10 24)) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77(7) - paragraph (3)(a) ceases to be in force on April 1, 1997 (src:1417)`

#ASSERT `reg 77(7) paragraph 77(3)(a) is in force on the day` (YMD 1996 7 1)
#ASSERT `reg 77(7) paragraph 77(3)(a) is in force on the day` (YMD 1997 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(7) paragraph 77(3)(a) is in force on the day` (YMD 1997 4 1))

§ `Reg 77(3) - eligibility (src:1405-1411)`

-- The argument order is: resides in Canada; the day eligibility is tested; initial claim; a claim to which s 26(2) applies; the period of eligibility; claims every week as (d) requires.
-- Every condition met: period of eligibility from June 30, 1996 to January 10, 1997.
#ASSERT `reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1996 12 1) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 6 30), (YMD 1997 1 10)) TRUE
-- (c): the period begins on June 29, 1996, the day before June 30, 1996: not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1996 12 1) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 6 29), (YMD 1997 1 10)) TRUE)
-- (c): the period ends on June 26, 1999, the last day allowed: eligible; the day after: not.
#ASSERT `reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1998 12 1) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1998 6 30), (YMD 1999 6 26)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1998 12 1) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1998 6 30), (YMD 1999 6 27)) TRUE)
-- (a): not resident in Canada, tested on March 31, 1997: not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` FALSE (YMD 1997 3 31) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 6 30), (YMD 1997 1 10)) TRUE)
-- (a) has ceased to be in force on April 1, 1997: not resident, tested that day, eligible.
#ASSERT `reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` FALSE (YMD 1997 4 1) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 4 1), (YMD 1998 1 10)) TRUE
-- (b): neither an initial claim nor a claim under s 26(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1996 12 1) FALSE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 6 30), (YMD 1997 1 10)) TRUE)
-- (b): a claim to which s 26(2) applies, not an initial claim.
#ASSERT `reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1996 12 1) FALSE TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 6 30), (YMD 1997 1 10)) TRUE
-- (d): not every week is claimed.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(3) the claimant is eligible to participate in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE (YMD 1996 12 1) TRUE FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1996 6 30), (YMD 1997 1 10)) FALSE)

§ `Reg 77(4) - the form and participation (src:1412-1414)`

-- The argument order is: completed and signed the form; the form records agreement (a); the form records agreement (b).
#ASSERT `reg 77(4) the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4) the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4) the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4) the claimant has signed the form with the agreements it requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The argument order is: eligible; wishes to participate; has signed the form.
#ASSERT `reg 77(4) the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4) the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4) the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4) the claimant participates in Pilot Project No. 1` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (b): the duty to notify arises for a participant who ceases to meet a condition whose failure reduces or eliminates benefits for a week.
#ASSERT `reg 77(4)(b) the claimant must notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4)(b) the claimant must notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4)(b) the claimant must notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- A condition whose failure changes no week's benefits does not trigger the duty.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(4)(b) the claimant must notify the Commission of the condition as soon as possible` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Reg 77(5) - deemed claims (src:1415)`

-- The argument order is: participates; the Sunday that begins the week; a week of unemployment; the period of eligibility (March 2 to August 2, 1997; March 2, 1997 is a Sunday).
-- The first week of the period: it starts on the first day of the period.
#ASSERT `reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` TRUE (YMD 1997 3 2) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 8 2))
-- The week of Sunday February 23, 1997 ends on Saturday March 1, 1997, before the period begins.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` TRUE (YMD 1997 2 23) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)))
-- The week of Sunday July 27, 1997 ends on Saturday August 2, 1997, the last day of the period.
#ASSERT `reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` TRUE (YMD 1997 7 27) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 8 2))
-- The week of Sunday August 3, 1997 is after the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` TRUE (YMD 1997 8 3) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)))
-- Not a participant; not a week of unemployment.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` FALSE (YMD 1997 3 9) TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77(5) the claimant is deemed to have made a claim for benefits for the week` TRUE (YMD 1997 3 9) FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 1997 3 2), (YMD 1997 8 2)))

§ `Reg 77(6) - the Commission may end participation (src:1416)`

-- The argument order is: the Commission becomes aware; the Commission decides to terminate; the day it becomes aware.
#ASSERT `reg 77(6) the day as of which the claimant's participation is terminated` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1997 5 5) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1997 5 5)
-- Aware but does not terminate: the power is not used.
#ASSERT `reg 77(6) the day as of which the claimant's participation is terminated` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1997 5 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not aware: no power.
#ASSERT `reg 77(6) the day as of which the claimant's participation is terminated` FALSE TRUE (YMD 1997 5 5) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.1(6) and (2) - the weeks and the claimants of Pilot Project No. 5 (src:1421-1430)`

-- The invented days: the section comes into force on Wednesday February 9, 2000 and ceases to have effect on Wednesday March 14, 2001; their weeks begin on Sundays February 6, 2000 and March 11, 2001.
-- The argument order is: the Sunday that begins the week; the day the section comes into force; the day it ceases to have effect.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(6) Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` (YMD 2000 2 6) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14)
-- The week before the week in which the section comes into force.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(6) Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` (YMD 2000 1 30) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14))
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(6) Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` (YMD 2001 3 11) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14)
-- The week after the week in which the section ceases to have effect.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(6) Pilot Project No. 5 applies to the week` (YMD 2001 3 18) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14))
-- The argument order of (2) is: the day the benefit period begins; the day it ends, if it has; the day the section comes into force; the day it ceases; indemnity payment; entitled for such a week.
-- The benefit period begins inside the project.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 2000 3 1) NOTHING (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE
-- The benefit period begins on the first day of the project, and on the last day.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 2000 2 9) NOTHING (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 2001 3 14) NOTHING (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE
-- The benefit period begins before the project and ends during it.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 1999 9 1) (JUST (YMD 2000 6 1)) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE
-- Begins and ends before the project.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 1999 1 1) (JUST (YMD 1999 12 31)) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE)
-- Begins before the project and has not ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 1999 9 1) NOTHING (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE)
-- Begins and ends after the project.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 2001 4 1) (JUST (YMD 2001 12 31)) (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE TRUE)
-- (b) and (c).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 2000 3 1) NOTHING (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 5` (YMD 2000 3 1) NOTHING (YMD 2000 2 9) (YMD 2001 3 14) TRUE FALSE)

§ `Reg 77.1(3) to (5) - choosing not to be paid (src:1425-1429)`

-- The argument order of (3) is: included; the project applies to the week; chooses not to be paid; chose after being paid; the Commission informed the claimant beforehand; rescinded.
-- A choice made before payment: deemed to have proved no entitlement for the week.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (4)(a): a choice after payment, the claimant having been informed beforehand: (3) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (4)(b): a choice after payment, not informed: (3) applies.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Rescinded.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not included; the project does not apply to the week; no choice.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(3) the claimant is deemed to have proved that they are not entitled to benefits for the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The argument order of (4)(b) is: included; chooses not to be paid after being paid; informed beforehand; rescinded.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(4)(b) the claimant must repay the benefits paid for the week` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (5): a claimant who made a choice and rescinds it is paid.
#ASSERT `reg 77.1(5) the claimant is to be paid the benefits to which they are entitled` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(5) the claimant is to be paid the benefits to which they are entitled` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.1(5) the claimant is to be paid the benefits to which they are entitled` FALSE TRUE)
